      "message": "Also, if you use a std::map then you could do something like this:\n\n```C++\n#define MAP_ITEM(N)  {N, #N},\nstatic std::map\u003cint, std::string\u003e my_map \u003d {\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_SUCCESS)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_COMMAND)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_ERROR)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_RESPONSE)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_VERSION)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_CHECKSUM)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_IN_PROGRESS)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_TIMEOUT)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_OVERFLOW)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_REQUEST_TRUNCATED)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_RESPONSE_TOO_BIG)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_BUS_ERROR)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_BUSY)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER_VERSION)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER_CRC)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_INVALID_DATA_CRC)\nMAP_ITEM(EC_RES_DUP_UNAVAILABLE)\n};\n```\n\nThe preprocessor would turn this into:\n```\nstatic std::map\u003cint, std::string\u003e my_map2 \u003d {\n\t{EC_RES_SUCCESS, \"EC_RES_SUCCESS\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_COMMAND, \"EC_RES_INVALID_COMMAND\"},\n\t{EC_RES_ERROR, \"EC_RES_ERROR\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM, \"EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM\"},\n\t{EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED, \"EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_RESPONSE, \"EC_RES_INVALID_RESPONSE\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_VERSION, \"EC_RES_INVALID_VERSION\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_CHECKSUM, \"EC_RES_INVALID_CHECKSUM\"},\n\t{EC_RES_IN_PROGRESS, \"EC_RES_IN_PROGRESS\"},\n\t{EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE, \"EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE\"},\n\t{EC_RES_TIMEOUT, \"EC_RES_TIMEOUT\"},\n\t{EC_RES_OVERFLOW, \"EC_RES_OVERFLOW\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER, \"EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER\"},\n\t{EC_RES_REQUEST_TRUNCATED, \"EC_RES_REQUEST_TRUNCATED\"},\n\t{EC_RES_RESPONSE_TOO_BIG, \"EC_RES_RESPONSE_TOO_BIG\"},\n\t{EC_RES_BUS_ERROR, \"EC_RES_BUS_ERROR\"},\n\t{EC_RES_BUSY, \"EC_RES_BUSY\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER_VERSION, \"EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER_VERSION\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER_CRC, \"EC_RES_INVALID_HEADER_CRC\"},\n\t{EC_RES_INVALID_DATA_CRC, \"EC_RES_INVALID_DATA_CRC\"},\n\t{EC_RES_DUP_UNAVAILABLE, \"EC_RES_DUP_UNAVAILABLE\"},\n};\n```\n\nThe printed result in a bit more verbose (it includes the `EC_RES` prefix) but it limits the potential for typos, etc.",
